course: dictionary
lesson: 12249
title: Formal words: constituted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some texts, like official letters and exam papers, use a stiff, formal voice with longer words. Constituted is one of them. Do not panic: the words around it usually give you the meaning.
explain: Constituted means made up or formed. «The club is constituted of twelve members.» The club is made up of twelve members, so constituted means made up. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The club is made up of twelve members" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Constituted can also mean counted as. «Finishing the race constituted a success.» Finishing the race counted as a success. Look for clues like a total, a whole, or a result, then swap your meaning in.
explain: Constituted can also mean set up officially, like a committee. «The committee was constituted last year.» It means the committee was formed in an official way. Maths texts may use it to show parts that make a whole: «Girls constituted half of the class» tells you that girls made up half the class.
fact: Constituted is the past form of the verb constitute.
fact: «Constituted» means made up or formed: «The club is constituted of twelve members.»
fact: «Constituted» can mean counted as: «Finishing the race constituted a success.»
fact: «Duly constituted» means set up properly and officially, like a club with proper rules.
fact: Formal words like constituted often appear in official letters and exams, so check the sentence around them for clues.
exercise: «The jury is constituted of twelve people.» What does constituted mean here? | Running late | *Made up of | Painted | Thrown out of
exercise: «Winning the match constituted a huge achievement.» What does constituted mean here? | *Counted as | Lost | Forgotten | Painted bright red
exercise: «The new committee was duly constituted last week.» What does duly constituted suggest? | Painted in bright colours | *Set up properly and officially | Broken and closed | Lost in the post
test: «Boys constituted a third of the chess club.» Which phrase means the same as constituted here? | Left out | Ran away from | *Made up
test: «The group was constituted by the school council.» What does it mean for a group to be constituted? | Made of wood | Sang loudly | Lost its way | *Set up officially
exam: «Four goals constituted victory for the home side.» Which meaning fits constituted best? | Hid from | Forgot about | *Counted as | Tripped over
